Saani, attached is twp_places_urban.dta .  It has TENDIGIT_FIPS and dummy v=
ariables for whether a township, village, or city is urban.

Urban is measured in two ways, both of which could be tried.

clusterdummy is a dummy variable that takes the value 1 if the municipality=
 is part of an urban cluster, like Ottawa city; it has to have at least a 0=
.30 allocation factor to an urban cluster in 2010.  These are not part of u=
rban areas, but they are clusters of urbanity isolated from urban areas

uadummy is a dummy variable that takes the value 1 if the municipality is p=
art of an urbanized area like Toledo city; it has to have at least a 0.30 a=
llocation factor to an urbanized area in 2010

Using just uadummy =3D 1 is the more restrictive way to measure being urban=
 ; adding clusterdummy =3D 1 is the more inclusive measure of being urban (=
urbanized areas + urban clusters)

David Brasington
Kautz Chair in Political Economy
Be excellent to each other, and party on, dudes. (Bill and Ted's Excellent =
Adventure)

